(A list a function returns keeps the texts its body proves it holds)
To 'the rows'.
    a list called rows is [].
    a buffer called digits is "12".
    a text called row is digits as text.
    append row to rows.
    append "3.5" to rows.
    Return a list, rows.

To 'the rows of' with a text called extra.
    a list called rows is ["40"].
    append extra to rows.
    Return a list, rows.

To 'the tally'.
    a list called tally is [1, 2].
    Return a list, tally.

a list called got is 'the rows'.
For each row in got,
    a float called 'parsed float' is row as a float,
    Print 'parsed float'.
a list called kept is [].
For each row in got, append row to kept.
Print "kept: {kept}".
a list called 'the extra rows' is 'the rows of' of "2".
For each row in 'the extra rows',
    a number called parsed is row as a number,
    Print parsed add 1.
a list called counts is 'the tally'.
For each count in counts, Print count add 1.
a list called widened is 'the rows'.
append 7 to widened.
Print "widened: {widened}".
To 'parse inside'.
    a list called 'rows inside' is 'the rows'.
    For each row in 'rows inside',
        a number called parsed is row as a number,
        Print "inside {parsed}".

'parse inside'.

To 'the single row'.
    a list called rows is ["12"].
    Return a list, rows.

a list called widened is 'the single row'.
append 7 to widened.
For each row in widened, Print "{row}".

(A list that does not start empty keeps its elements' own types when a number is appended)
To 'the lone row'.
    a list called 'row list' is ["12"].
    Return a list, 'row list'.

a list called 'plain rows' is 'the lone row'.
For each row in 'plain rows', Print "plain {row}".
a list called 'widened rows' is 'the lone row'.
append 7 to 'widened rows'.
For each row in 'widened rows', Print "widened {row}".
For each row in 'widened rows', Print row.
Print 'widened rows'.

(A list parameter holds the caller's elements before its first append)
To 'add a word to' with a list called items.
    append "word" to items.
    For each item in items, Print "item {item}".

a list called counts is [1, 2].
'add a word to' of counts.

(Lists named from a parameter, written by element, or handed to another function read each element as what it is)
To 'tagged copy of' with a list called items.
    a list called out is items.
    append "x" to out.
    Return a list, out.

a list called 'tagged copies' is 'tagged copy of' of [1, 2].
For each entry in 'tagged copies', Print entry.

To 'set rows'.
    a list called out is [].
    append "x" to out.
    append "y" to out.
    Set element 1 of out to 5.
    Return a list, out.

a list called 'set entries' is 'set rows'.
For each entry in 'set entries', Print entry.

To 'add a number' with a list called target.
    append 7 to target.

To 'handed rows'.
    a list called out is [].
    append "y" to out.
    'add a number' of out.
    Return a list, out.

a list called 'handed entries' is 'handed rows'.
For each entry in 'handed entries', Print entry.
